      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Auto mode is now the default in Claude Code",
      "url": "https://claude.com/blog/auto-mode-default-in-claude-code",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49239021",
      "score": 269,
      "comments": 291,
      "author": "sbehere",
      "published": "2026-08-10T03:50:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Anthropic made Auto mode the default in Claude Code CLI, executing shell commands and file edits without per-action human approval.",
        "The default autonomous execution speeds up developer workflows but heightens security risks around unattended command and script runs.",
        "AI engineering teams should implement OS sandboxing or permission boundaries to safely manage Anthropic's increasingly autonomous agentic CLI."
      ]
    },
